  "summary": "A venturi tube measures flow with a smooth convergent cone, a short cylindrical throat and a gentle divergent cone. Pressure falls in the throat as velocity rises (Bernoulli), and the long diffuser recovers most of it, so permanent pressure loss is very low — ideal for large water mains and energy-sensitive services. It also tolerates dirty fluids better than an orifice (ISO 5167-4).",
  "classification": {
